-- title:
--   Crossing chart coordinates have order one on both components
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M$ with $p \mid M$, $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit whose image in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$ is $1$, and the hypothesis $hj$ that $jqModC$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ lies in the $q$-expansion function field of the full modular group; let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model package `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and $\rho : R_p \to A$ a lift of the structure map $R_p \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain with $\rho_O : R_p \to O$, maximal ideal generated by $p$, equipped with: a surjective $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa_A$ compatible with $\rho$ and the residue map, a map $j_O : O \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ over $R_p$, and $\iota_A : O \to A$ inducing $j_O$ and $\mathrm{to}\kappa$. Let $n$ be a point of the fibre product of the two component maps $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,0$ and $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,1$ (a crossing of the special fibre), and write $x_n$ for its image in `XO (ΓM M H) hj ρO` along `pullback.fst` followed by $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,0$ and `bcMap`. Assume given $e \ge 1$, an open $U \ni x_n$ of `XO (ΓM M H) hj ρO`, and a morphism $f : U \to \operatorname{Spec} O[x_0,x_1]/(x_0x_1 - p^e)$ such that: $f$ composed with the structure map to $\operatorname{Spec} O$ is the inclusion of $U$ followed by the projection to $\operatorname{Spec} O$; the classes $u$ and $v$ of the two coordinates lie simultaneously in the prime $f(y)$ exactly when $y$ maps to $x_n$; at every such $y$ the stalk map of $f$ is flat, carries the maximal ideal onto the maximal ideal, and induces an isomorphism of residue fields, and $f$ is étale on some open neighbourhood of $y$ in $U$; and $v \in f(y)$ holds precisely when $y$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,0$ composed with `bcMap`, while $u \in f(y)$ holds precisely when $y$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,1$ composed with `bcMap` (the four implications stated separately). Put $g_v, g_u \in \Gamma(\,\mathrm{XO}, U)$ for the pullbacks along $f$ of the global sections corresponding to $v$ and $u$ (auxiliary objects $XQ$, $prJ$ and $VM$ are introduced along the way). The conclusion, for the integral special-fibre curve model $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Mfib}$, is twofold: its generic point lies in the preimage of $U$ under $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{efib}$ composed with $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,1$ and `bcMap`, and the order at the place `placeOn1` attached to $n$ of the function-field element obtained (through `ffEquiv.symm`) from the germ at that generic point of the pullback of $g_v$ equals $1$; and symmetrically with $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\,0$, $g_u$ and `placeOn0`, the order there also being $1$. Here the order of a place is $-\log$ of its adic valuation, so each assertion says the relevant function is a uniformiser at the place.
--
--   This is the clause of the Deligne–Rapoport node analysis saying that the two coordinates of an étale crossing chart $x_0x_1 = p^e$ at a supersingular crossing restrict on the two components of the special fibre to uniformisers at the corresponding places, the normalisation that attaches the node annulus to the two components. It feeds the construction of the annulus around the crossing with its parameter and modulus $p^e$, and the construction of sections with prescribed orders at crossings.
